A pure kernel shared by UI, API and evals:
- the lifecycle graph;
- 10 ConsentScopes;
- activeConsentScopes (current policy, unrevoked, unexpired, not future-dated);
- activationReadiness with typed blockers such as consent_missing:<scope> and eval_not_passed:<suite>;
- server-chosen UUID object paths;
- assertContentFreeAuditFacts (forbidden keys, scalars of at most 200 characters).

The ten laws:
- layers, never one prompt;
- evidence and inference are different types;
- the base person and the relationship are different;
- providers are replaceable;
- consent is a capability;
- every output declares itself;
- noisy input is never cleaned into certainty;
- calibration produces preferences, not prompt accretion;
- activation freezes a capability;
- extraction proposes, the owner disposes.
The north star is fidelity = voice x delivery x behaviour x autobiography x relational x consent.
